{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2022 AMC 10B #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">2022 AMC 12B #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Generalization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Generalization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Detailed_Explanation_of_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Detailed Explanation of Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Simple_Sums)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Simple Sums)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Educated_Guess)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Educated Guess)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(1-16)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(1-16)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math4All999\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math4All999</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many of the first ten numbers of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff42b81a765f0bbad70b9c2307e27d5875ecd52b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121, 11211, 1112111, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"17\" /> are prime numbers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/4688386b300aae1e7b697b04f74822910b366810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Generalization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Generalization)\">Solution 1 (Generalization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Generalization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf008a137d87ab45db52ff31596b992c286d309d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 121 &amp;= 110 + 11, \\\\ 11211 &amp;= 11100 + 111, \\\\ 1112111 &amp;= 1111000 + 1111, \\\\ &amp; \\ \\vdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"212\" height=\"102\" />\nWe generate the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th term of this sequence:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b8d71075dff9c87a43c0c4dd2d32c4c3b1415d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=n}^{2n}10^k + \\sum_{k=0}^{n}10^k = 10^n\\sum_{k=0}^{n}10^k + \\sum_{k=0}^{n}10^k = \\left(10^n+1\\right)\\sum_{k=0}^{n}10^k.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"51\" />\nIt follows that the terms are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c94489bf5a94af523902528cb6f8d31e305fe7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 121 &amp;= 11\\cdot11, \\\\ 11211 &amp;= 101\\cdot111, \\\\ 1112111 &amp;= 1001\\cdot1111, \\\\ &amp; \\ \\vdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"176\" height=\"102\" />\nTherefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d23afde92b8d87cebc50411cc3aeb0d3b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> prime numbers in this sequence.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Detailed_Explanation_of_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Detailed_Explanation_of_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (Detailed Explanation of Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Detailed Explanation of Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote this sequence as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, then we can find that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a976ea6ab7856876405ddfd144f96254430464f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_{1} &amp;= 121 = 10^2 + 2\\cdot10 + 1 = (10^2 + 10) + (10 + 1), \\\\ a_{2} &amp;= 11211 = (10^4 + 10^3 + 10^2) + (10^2 + 10 + 1), \\\\ a_{3} &amp;= 1112111 = (10^6 + 10^5 + 10^4 + 10^3) + (10^3 + 10^2 + 10 + 1), \\\\ &amp; \\ \\vdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"497\" height=\"111\" />\nSo, we can induct that the general term is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b4e4ef905e8708420e58261b47cb41b60f739f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_n &amp;= (10^{2n} + 10^{2n-1} + \\ldots + 10^{n+1} + 10^n) + (10^n + 10^{n-1} + \\ldots +10 + 1) \\\\ &amp;= 10^n\\cdot(10^n + 10^{n-1} + \\ldots +10 + 1) + (10^n + 10^{n-1} + \\ldots +10 + 1) \\\\ &amp;= \\left(10^n+1\\right)\\sum_{k=0}^{n}10^k. \\end{align*}\" width=\"566\" height=\"105\" />\nTherefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d23afde92b8d87cebc50411cc3aeb0d3b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> prime numbers in this sequence.\n</p><p>~PythZhou\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Simple_Sums.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Simple_Sums)\">Solution 3 (Simple Sums)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Simple Sums)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe how \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/0/bf008a137d87ab45db52ff31596b992c286d309d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 121 &amp;= 110 + 11, \\\\ 11211 &amp;= 11100 + 111, \\\\ 1112111 &amp;= 1111000 + 1111, \\\\ &amp; \\ \\vdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"212\" height=\"102\" />\nall take the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d28c89dde00e4db0f9c285ddb1dbec2edb4f2a96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\underbrace{111\\ldots}_{n+1}\\underbrace{00\\ldots}_{n} + \\underbrace{111\\ldots}_{n+1} = \\underbrace{111\\ldots}_{n+1}(10^{n} + 1).\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"37\" />\nFactoring each of the sums, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f92bf0e88c9fd5624d4a464589723aab6a048b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[11(10+1), 111(100+1), 1111(1000+1), \\ldots\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. With each number factored, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a054d23afde92b8d87cebc50411cc3aeb0d3b401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> primes in the set.\n</p><p>~ab2024\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Educated_Guess.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Educated_Guess)\">Solution 4 (Educated Guess)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Educated Guess)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ad7692f5d86be790209a56a68c2a3488235054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d386f5fadc134dc15e2f8599565665895a84574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11211$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Because this is Problem 6 of the AMC 10 or Problem 3 on the AMC 12, we assume we do not need to check two-digit prime divisibility or use obscure theorems. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/0210e480bd3f42a6fd24d5ff8c073a1b83eddebb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 0}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"63\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>Note: This is an assumption and not a suggested solution. However, it could be useful as a last resort.\n</p><p>~Dhillonr25\n-Note by XaberTooth\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.281-16.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(1-16)\">Video Solution(1-16)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(1-16)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SCwQ9jUfr0g\">https://youtu.be/SCwQ9jUfr0g</a>\n</p><p>~~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_KNR0JV5rdI?t=562\">https://youtu.be/_KNR0JV5rdI?t=562</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math4All999\">Video Solution by Math4All999</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math4All999\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5QYh3hNaDa0?feature=shared\">https://youtu.be/5QYh3hNaDa0?feature=shared</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Ani_lytical\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DnydjTStcWU?si=7pfh_4Q7RG3BbL1J\">https://youtu.be/DnydjTStcWU?si=7pfh_4Q7RG3BbL1J</a>\n</p><p>~Ani_lytical\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B\">2022 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" clas