p>n\n+\n1\nn+1 ones, and \n10\nn\n+\n1\n10 \nn\n</p>\n<pre>+1 is also greater than \n</pre>\n<p>1\n1 for all \nn\n≥\n1\nn≥1.\n</p><p>So every term factors into two integers greater than \n1\n1, meaning every term is composite.\n</p><p>Therefore, among the first ten terms, the number of primes is\n</p><p>0\n.\n0\n</p>\n<pre>.\n</pre></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018004822\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.078 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 302/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 4468/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 415/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4680/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   29.439      1 -total\n 27.31%    8.041      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 24.80%    7.302      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 18.56%    5.465      1 Template:Duplicate\n 16.28%    4.792      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23361:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018004822 and revision id 293282. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}